; XSpark - XAUUSD M5 "reachable targets" profile
; STATUS: UNTESTED HYPOTHESIS. No Strategy Tester run has been performed on this
; preset. The reasoning below is measured; the outcome is not. Test before use.
;
; PROBLEM THIS ADDRESSES
; The 810-trade run of xauusd-m5-survival.set produced a 19.01% win rate against
; an 80.99% loss rate, PF 0.94, and 38 consecutive losses. Two measured causes:
;
; 1. THE PARTIAL CLOSE IS THE WIN-RATE ENGINE, AND IT WAS DISABLED.
;    In the earlier 3%-risk run, 81.5% of ALL winning positions involved a
;    partial close. Positions that fired a partial won 96.5% of the time;
;    positions that did not won 7.1%.
;    That run's deals/trades ratio was 2.25 (partials firing). The survival
;    run's was exactly 2.00 - zero partials fired, in 810 trades.
;    Cause: LegalPartialCloseVolume() returns 0 when a 50% close would leave a
;    residual below SYMBOL_VOLUME_MIN. At 0.35% risk on $5,000 with a 3.0 x ATR
;    stop, every position sizes to the 0.01 minimum, so no partial is ever legal.
;    The threshold is ~0.37% risk at ATR 3.1 - the survival preset sat just under
;    the cliff at 0.35%.
;
; 2. THE TARGETS WERE UNREACHABLE.
;    With InpATRMultSL=3.0 and InpMaxRR=10.0, the median planned target was 6.94R
;    - about 21 ATR of M5 gold movement. Only 2.6% of positions ever exceeded 4R.
;    A 7:1 reward:risk geometry cannot produce a high win rate: even with no edge
;    at all, expected win rate is ~1/(1+7) = 12.5%.
;
; WHAT THIS CHANGES
; Stop and target geometry back to the EA's shipped defaults, which were never
; actually tested. Effect is twofold:
;   - Target:stop ratio moves from ~7:1 to ~3:1, so targets are reachable.
;   - A 1.5 x ATR stop is half as wide, so the same risk % buys ~2x the lots,
;     lifting size clear of the 0.02-lot floor and re-enabling partial closes.
;     At 0.5% risk on $5,000, ATR 3.1: ~0.05 lots. At ATR 6.0: ~0.02 lots.
;     Above roughly ATR 10 the partial goes illegal again - watch for it.
;
; HONEST EXPECTATION
; This should raise win rate, because win rate is mostly a function of the
; target:stop ratio. It does NOT by itself create edge - a tighter target earns
; less per win. Whether expectancy improves is exactly what the test decides.
; Note also that a narrower stop makes the fixed spread a larger fraction of R,
; so costs rise as a share of risk.

InpEnableTrading=true
InpEntryStyle=0
InpAutoTuneForSymbol=true
InpMinScore=3.0

; --- sizing: conservative, and kept clear of the 0.02-lot partial-close floor ---
InpMaxOpenTrades=2
InpRiskPctTier1=0.5
InpRiskPctTier2=0.5
InpRiskPctTier3=0.5
InpMaxRiskPct=0.75
InpMaxAccountRiskPct=1.5

; --- safety rails stay armed ---
InpMaxDailyDDPct=6.0
InpUseTotalDDKillSwitch=true
InpMaxTotalDDPct=25.0

; --- THE CHANGE: shipped-default stop/target geometry, reachable targets ---
InpATRMultSL=1.5
InpMinRR=1.5
InpMaxRR=3.0
InpPartialTPRatio=2.5
InpPartialClosePct=50.0
InpATRMultTrail=2.0

InpUsePinBars=true
InpPatternMaxChaseATR=0.5
